ope are the titular Sparks they  resemble the stars from Super Mario  Galaxy but their faces have been  completely replaced by rabbits because  of course they have by collecting the  means that you can use their own special  abilities to enhance your combat skills  and there are dozens of different Sparks  to rescue barks of Hope is coming  exclusively to switch on October 20th  finally a gross looking game to fit  October's spooky Vibes ebb software's  scorn in gamespot's latest preview of  the game Jordan ramay wrote quote in  scorn you play as an unnamed person who  has become isolated in an unnerving  place where vicious looking living  tissue and twisted mechanical  Contraptions have been combined in an  uncanny relationship that seems  symbiotic in nature there are some  moments of first person shooting and  elements of horror in scorn but the game  is more focused on puzzle solving and  exploration not action or scares this  game seems to push its player towards  exploration and organic Discovery rather  than explain where to go and what to do  so if that's your favorite type of  experience you can uncover the mystery  when scoring Launches on Xbox series X  and S and PC on October 21st the game  will also launch day one on Xbox game  pass  Bruce Wayne is dead however not all hope  is lost and Gotham Knights you take  control of the bat family as they go  head to head with the seediest of the  city's underbelly in practice this means  players choose from one of four  characters Nightwing red hood Batgirl or  Robin you can play either alone or with  one friend in two-player Co-op because  despite four character options the story  is without a four player mode with a  similar free flow combat to the Arkham  games Gotham Knights looks a lot like  those beloved games but will seek to  give each hero their own flourishes you  can make Bruce Wayne proud on October  21st when Gotham Knight's releases on  PS5 series X and S and PC  and Bayonetta 3 the Umbra which teams up  with familiar faces as well as a new one  named Viola in order to put an end to  the terror of the mysterious evil known  as the homunculi these new baddies are  considered man-made bioweapons and  according to Viola hope for defeating  them lies with the scientists named  siegerd when it comes to the gameplay  fans of the Bayonetta series should be  very familiar with moves like witch time  and torture attack but part 3 will  introduce some new moves one of which is  called demon masquerade a move that  allows Bayonetta to unleash even more  magic power by fusing with an infernal  demon the other is called the demon  slave and this lets Bayonetta control  demons from a distance for some welcome  help in battle this feature is different  yet similar to the summoning of  Bayonetta 1 and 2. a major addition to  the Bayonetta series is what Platinum  games has named naive Angel mode and  according to the company it is a  revolutionary feature that will allow  more people to fully enjoy it while the  mode is off Bayonetta will be fully nude  with some sensitive areas covered up by  her magic hair whereas when the mode is  on she'll simply be wearing her full  outfit Bayonetta 3 is releasing  exclusively for switch on October 28th  a plague tail Requiem is an  action-adventure stealth game that takes  place shortly after the events of the  first game a plague tale innocence like  the original you play as amicia a young  girl tasked with escorting her younger  brother Hugo through a plague-stricken  world infested with rats and accompanied  by hostile soldiers along with amicia's  trusty slang Requiem introduces a  crossbow however like in innocence most  encounters will still call for a  stealthier approach you can throw  objects to attract the enemies attention  squeeze under tight spaces to hide from  View and track your enemies movements  with a vision Mode called rat sense new  to a plague tale Requiem is the ability  to directly control a horde of rats and  turn any enemy who dared to venture away  from an open flame into a snack become  king of the rats when Requiem releases  on PS5 Xbox series X and s switch and PC  on October 18th Dragon Ball the breakers  pits seven non powered human characters  AKA survivors against one player  controlled iconic villain from across  the Dragon Ball Universe the seven  humans must survive until the end of the  match using items and perks against the  villain who wins by eliminating all  other players the first three playable  villains include cell Boo and Frieza  whether you're playing as one of them or  as a Survivor you get to choose a  progression path unlock perks and  customize your character using skins the  breakers features a large map with  several areas of interest that can be  destroyed by the Raiders as they hunt  you down luckily the survivors have  weapons vehicles and grappling hooks to  increase their chance of escaping see  how long you can survive when Dragon  Ball the breakers releases on every  console and PC on October 14th  EA's professional ice hockey simulation  series returns to the ice this October  with NHL 23 and it promises some changes  and improvements over last year's game  one of the biggest updates for NHL 23  are Last Chance moves when players  stumble on the ice they can perform  desperation moves like shooting and  passing from their knees according to EA  more than 500 Last Chance moves have  been added to NHL 23. additionally AI  goalies are better and smarter and they  also have an increased library of  desperation save animations in total  there are around 350 new save animations  including more active and acrobatic  animations than past games and in at  first for the NHL series cross play  matchmaking is coming to NHL 23. the  feature won't be there in time for  launch but is expected to arrive in a  November update lace up your skates and  get back on the ice on October 14th when  NHL 2 23 drops on PC and every console  except switch  I guess you can say I've left the  spookiest for last because the final  game on our list is the winter expansion  for Resident Evil Village this DLC  features an all-new story called Shadows  of rose that takes place after the main  village campaign you take control of  Rose Winters as she seeks to rid herself  of powers unlike the main game shadow of  Rose is exclusively in the third person  perspective putting it more in line with  the remakes of Resident Evil 2 and 3.  this DLC is coming to PC stadia and  every console except switch on October  28th switch owners will have the  pleasure of playing a cloud version of  the main village campaign on that same  day and if that wasn't enough Resident  Evil releases for the 28th reverse is  coming to PS4 Xbox One and PC on that  same day  so which of these games are you most  interested in and are there any that you  can't wait to play that didn't make the  list let us know in the comments you can  follow me on Twitter at Devonte Chisholm  and make sure you're subscribed to  Gamespot for more  [Music]
 

